  "summary": "The paper proposes a single-qubit-based deep quantum neural network for credit card fraud detection, using MSFLA feature selection and 10-fold cross-validation on the Kaggle European credit card fraud dataset (284,807 transactions, 491 fraud cases). The proposed model reports 97.06% accuracy, 96.94% F1-score, 96.67% recall, and 97.23% precision, outperforming the listed classical baselines (ELM, DBN, LSTM, RNN, CNN) on these metrics, but no runtime or quantum advantage analysis is provided.",
